      </script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://serply.io"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What do I get back?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"JSON. Results arrive parsed into fields such as title, link, and description, so you are reading a response rather than writing selectors against a page that changes. Page Fetch can also return markdown instead of HTML."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to deal with proxies or CAPTCHAs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Proxy rotation, retries, and CAPTCHA handling happen behind the endpoint. That is the part that breaks when you build search scraping yourself, and it is the part you are handing over."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use this from an MCP client?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We host one at https://api.serply.io/mcp: add it to Claude, Cursor, or any MCP-compatible client with your API key and the model can search and fetch pages as tool calls. Each tool call costs one credit, the same as a REST request. If you would rather run your own, the server on this page is about thirty lines."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does markdown matter for an AI pipeline?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"HTML spends most of its tokens on navigation, scripts, and styling that a model has to read and discard. Markdown keeps the headings, links, and prose and drops the rest, so more of the context window goes to the content you actually retrieved."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I search as a specific country or device?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. X-Proxy-Location takes any of fourteen countries including the US, UK, Germany, Japan, India, Brazil, and Australia, and X-User-Agent switches between desktop and mobile. Results differ between the two, so rank tracking needs both to be explicit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What replaced the Bing Search API?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Microsoft retired the Bing Search APIs on 11 August 2025 and directed developers to a wider Azure platform rather than a drop-in endpoint. Serply's /v1/b/search returns Bing organic results, text ads, and shopping ads as JSON over the same key and headers as every other endpoint here."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can this replace the Google Custom Search JSON API?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Google has closed the Custom Search JSON API to new customers and ends it on January 1, 2027. Serply returns Google results as JSON with no search engine ID, so most migrations are a new URL, a header for the key, and a few renamed fields."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free tier?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every new account gets 2,500 free credits with no card, good for 30 days. One credit is one successful request on any endpoint, MCP included, and cached responses are free. After that, prepaid packs start at $5 and those credits never expire."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which languages are supported?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Any language that can make an HTTP request. It is a REST API with a header for the key, so cURL, Python, JavaScript, Go, Ruby, and PHP all work with no SDK required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is this different from running my own scraper?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A scraper is cheap to write and expensive to keep alive. Layouts change, IPs get blocked, and CAPTCHAs appear at the worst time. Here that maintenance is the product."}}]}</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/nav-link.CN78G6nB.css"><style>.rotator[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]{vertical-align:bottom;text-align:left;display:inline-block;position:relative}.rotator-sizer[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]{visibility:hidden}.rotator-word[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]{opacity:0;animation:9s infinite rotate-word;position:absolute;inset:0}.rotator-word[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]:nth-child(2){animation-delay:0s}.rotator-word[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]:nth-child(3){animation-delay:3s}.rotator-word[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]:nth-child(4){animation-delay:6s}@keyframes rotate-word{0%{opacity:0;transform:translateY(.25em)}3%,30%{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}33%,to{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-.25em)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.rotator-word[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]{opacity:0;animation:none;transform:none}.rotator-word[data-astro-cid-lcdefpme]:nth-child(2){opacity:1}}
</style></head><body class="flex flex-col h-full"><noscript><iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-KHD2H2R" height="0" width="0" style="display: none; visibility: hidden"></iframe></noscript><!-- JSON-LD Structured Data --><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"Google Search API for AI Agents - Serply.io","description":"Real-time Google search, news, and maps as clean JSON or markdown. One REST API for agents, RAG, and MCP servers. Free tier, no credit card required.","url":"https://serply.io","image":"https://serply.io/google-search-api-serp.png","publisher":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"Serply, Inc.","url":"https://serply.io","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://serply.io/favicon/android-chrome-512x512.png"},"sameAs":["https://twitter.com/serply_io"],"contactPoint":{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"Customer Support","url":"https://serply.io/support"}}}</script><div class="flex h-screen flex-col justify-between"><style>astro-island,astro-slot,astro-static-slot{display:contents}</style><script>(()=>{var l=(n,t)=>{let i=async()=>{await(await n())()},e=typeof t.value=="object"?t.value:void 0,s={timeout:e==null?void 0:e.timeout};"requestIdleCallback"in window?window.requestIdleCallback(i,s):setTimeout(i,s.timeout||200)};(self.Astro||(self.Astro={})).idle=l;window.dispatchEvent(new Event("astro:idle"));})();</script><script>(()=>{var g=Object.defineProperty;var w=(a,s,c)=>s in a?g(a,s,{enumerable:!0,configurable:!0,writable:!0,value:c}):a[s]=c;var l=(a,s,c)=>w(a,typeof s!="symbol"?s+"":s,c);var E=new Set(["__proto__","constructor","prototype"]);{let a={0:t=>y(t),1:t=>c(t),2:t=>new RegExp(t),3:t=>new Date(t),4:t=>new Map(c(t)),5:t=>new Set(c(t)),6:t=>BigInt(t),7:t=>new URL(t),8:t=>new Uint8Array(t),9:t=>new Uint16Array(t),10:t=>new Uint32Array(t),11:t=>Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY*t},s=t=>{let[p,e]=t;return p in a?a[p](e):void 0},c=t=>t.map(s),y=t=>type